## 1.1 Zero-cost hosting

The product must remain usable without requiring paid infrastructure.

The owner explicitly requires a zero-VND hosting approach.

Use the existing GitHub Pages deployment as the first production hosting solution.

The current project already has a successful static deployment workflow. Preserve and improve it.

Do not migrate to Cloudflare, Render, Railway, Vercel, Netlify, or another hosting provider merely because it is familiar.

A migration is permitted only if you establish a concrete technical limitation that cannot reasonably be solved with the existing GitHub Pages deployment.

Do not introduce:

- Paid VPS hosting.
- Paid domains.
- Paid databases.
- Paid image-processing APIs.
- Paid AI inference APIs.
- Paid authentication services.
- Paid analytics.
- Subscription services.
- Unnecessary backend infrastructure.

