## 1.2 No continuously running personal computer

The owner must not need to keep a MacBook, NUC, NAS, Raspberry Pi, or another personal device running.

The deployed application must be served by managed hosting.

Local computers are only development environments.

Once deployment succeeds, the owner must be able to shut down all personal computers while friends continue accessing the public application.

## 1.3 Guest-first, local-first

Users must be able to use the primary features without creating an account.

Do not introduce mandatory registration or login.

Default behavior:

- Face analysis runs in the browser.
- Color analysis runs in the browser.
- Virtual try-on runs in the browser.
- Personal preferences remain local.
- Analysis history remains local.
- Saved products remain local.
- No automatic cloud synchronization.
- No automatic selfie upload.

Clearly explain that locally stored data belongs to the current browser/device and does not automatically synchronize between devices.

Provide data deletion controls.

## 1.4 Product quality over feature count

The objective is not to maximize the number of features.

The objective is to make existing features reliable, understandable, useful, and pleasant to use.

Do not add speculative AI functionality just to make the application appear more advanced.

